  "name": "Classify form leads with DeepSeek and route priority-based approvals to Sheets",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -980,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1060,
        "content": "## Classify form leads with DeepSeek, score priority, and route approvals to Sheets\n\n### How it works\n\nA webhook receives the form POST from any form builder and a Code node normalizes the submission: it trims whitespace, lowercases the email, and builds a deterministic lead_unique_id from the email and company name. A Data Table node then checks whether that lead has been processed before, so repeated form submissions and duplicate clicks skip the pipeline instead of spamming your approvers. Every new lead is recorded in the Data Table audit log, then sent to the DeepSeek API, which parses the raw text into structured fields and scores the lead priority from 1 to 100. A three-way Switch routes by score: high-priority leads get an approval email, medium leads get a fast-track approval email, and low-priority leads get a polite decline email instead of touching your fulfillment queue. Approved leads land in a Google Sheets fulfillment queue through a second webhook, and any LLM failure triggers a critical alert email instead of a silently dropped lead.\n\n### Video walkthrough\n\n@[youtube](XUon1HDxXM0)\n\n### Setup\n\n- Point your lead form at the lead-intake webhook URL and ensure it POSTs raw_client_input plus selected_service.\n- Create a Data Table with a lead_unique_id text column, then select it in both Data Table nodes and paste the column id into the Mark Processed node.\n- Create a Header Auth credential for the DeepSeek API with Authorization as the header name, then select it in the Classify and Score Lead node.\n- Connect Gmail credentials for approval, fast-track, decline and alert emails, and replace YOUR_EMAIL@example.com in all four email nodes.\n- Connect Google Sheets, replace YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID, and replace YOUR_N8N_WEBHOOK_DOMAIN in the approval emails with your n8n instance base URL."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Capture Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -340,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Capture and deduplicate\n\nThe webhook receives the form submission, the Code node normalizes fields and builds lead_unique_id, and the Data Table gate passes only leads never processed before."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Score Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -340,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Audit, classify and score\n\nThe audit-log node records the lead, DeepSeek parses the raw text into structured fields and returns a 1-100 priority score with structured output."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0004-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Route Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Route by priority\n\nThe three-way Switch sends high scores to the normal approval email, medium scores to a fast-track approval, and low scores to a polite decline email that never touches the fulfillment queue."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0005-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Fulfill Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Approval gate and fulfillment\n\nThe approval webhook validates the decision, appends approved leads to the Google Sheets fulfillment queue, and returns a styled HTML confirmation page. LLM failures bypass everything and raise an alert email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "When Form Lead Submitted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        -220,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0007-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Normalize Lead Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        0,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Normalize the incoming lead and build a deterministic dedup key\nconst body = $input.item.json.body || {};\nconst email = String(body.email || '').trim().toLowerCase();\nconst company = String(body.company_name || body.raw_client_input || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ');\nconst unique = email + '|' + company;\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...body,\n    email,\n    company_name: body.company_name || '',\n    lead_unique_id: unique,\n    received_at: $now.toISO()\n  }\n};"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0008-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Check Lead Not Processed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        220,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "lead_unique_id",
              "keyValue": "={{ $json.lead_unique_id }}",
              "condition": "eq"
            }
          ]
        },
        "resource": "row",
        "matchType": "anyCondition",
        "operation": "rowNotExists",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_DATA_TABLE_ID",
          "cachedResultName": "Lead Intake - Processed Leads"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0009-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Mark Lead Processed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        440,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "email": "={{ $json.email }}",
            "status": "received",
            "first_seen": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
            "company_name": "={{ $json.company_name }}",
            "lead_unique_id": "={{ $json.lead_unique_id }}",
            "selected_service": "={{ $json.selected_service }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "manual"
        },
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "key_id": "YOUR_LEAD_UNIQUE_ID_COLUMN_ID",
              "keyName": "lead_unique_id",
              "keyValue": "={{ $json.lead_unique_id }}",
              "condition": "eq"
            }
          ]
        },
        "resource": "row",
        "matchType": "anyCondition",
        "operation": "upsert",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_DATA_TABLE_ID",
          "cachedResultName": "Lead Intake - Processed Leads"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0010-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Classify and Score Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        660,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify( { model: \"deepseek-chat\", messages: [ { role: \"system\", content: \"You are the lead qualification agent for a business services intake form. Parse the raw client submission into structured data and estimate the lead priority. Output raw JSON only, no markdown. Fields: company_name, state, owner, priority_score (integer 1-100 where 90+ means enterprise-ready client with a clear project, 60-89 means qualified small business, below 60 means low-fit or incomplete submission), reason (one sentence justifying the score).\" }, { role: \"user\", content: \"Parse and score this client submission: \" + JSON.stringify($('When Form Lead Submitted').item.json.body) } ], temperature: 0.1, response_format: { type: \"json_object\" } } ) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.4
    },
    {
      "id": "a1e2b3c4-0011-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Extract LLM Response Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        880,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Parse the LLM response into structured fields and attach the dedup key\nconst raw = $input.item.json.choices[0].message.content;\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\nconst prev = $('Normalize Lead Data').item.json;\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    company_name: parsed.company_name || prev.company_name || '',\n    state: parsed.state || '',\n    owner: parsed.owner || '',\n    priority_score: Number(parsed.priority_score || 0),\n    reason: parsed.reason || '',\n    lead_unique_id: prev.lead_unique_id,\n    email: prev.email\n  }\n};"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
